# Scout — what git tracks vs what it must never see.
#
# TRACKED: code (cmd/, pkg/), workspace TEMPLATE (pkg/workspace/template/),
# docs (docs/, README.md), config EXAMPLE (config/config.example.json),
# scripts, Makefile, go.mod/go.sum, LICENSE.
#
# NEVER TRACKED: anything from a live install —
# - databases (*.db*) and WAL files
# - secret material (.env*, .masterkey, config.json with keys)
# - user workspace copies (~/.local/share/scout/workspace — outside the repo)
# - shell history, CV uploads, logs, build output, binaries

# Binaries and build output
/scout
/scout-*
/bin/
/dist/
/build/
*.exe
*.test

# Databases (local-first SQLite)
/*.db
/*.db-wal
/*.db-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Secrets & config with keys — the lock must never travel with the safe.
.env
.env.*
.masterkey
**/.master-key
config.json
.secrets.json

# User material that must stay on the device
*.log
*.pdf
cv*.txt
resume*.txt
history

# OS
.DS_Store

# Build-time coding-agent aids (not part of Scout)
.pi/
